From 790bfbe16a977ead6db5b8c127a45fdc32d2f9ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:21:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] workspace: Remove the outputs at teardown as at run time

~Workspace emitted outputRemoved for each output while outputs() and
outputOrder() still listed every output, and unreferenced each output
right after its own signal. A listener that answers by walking the
workspace's outputs, as the StereoDepth D-Bus interface does since
18e9430, read at the second signal an output already freed, and KWin
crashed at exit now and then: testScreenshotStereo ended with a
segmentation fault after all its tests passed in 3 of 55 runs of the
+stereo3d39 test build.

The outputs are now taken out of the list first and out of the output
order, and unreferenced only after the last outputRemoved, as
updateOutputs() does for an output that went away.

testWorkspaceTeardown watches outputRemoved while the workspace of two
outputs is destroyed: the removed output is listed by neither
outputs() nor outputOrder(), and no output is freed before the last
signal.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
